<title>PERU: Peru's September tin output rises 20.9 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's September tin output rises 20.9 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's tin output rose 20.9 percent to 2,293 tonnes in September, compared with the same month last year, according to preliminary figures from the Energy and Mines Ministry released Tuesday.</p>
<p>Production rose 25.6 percent to 19,635 tonnes in the first nine months of the year, compared with the same period last year, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Peru's tin production rose 10.1 percent to 22,331 tonnes in 1995 compared with 20,275 tonnes the previous year.</p>
<p>Minsur is the world's third largest tin producer. The company operates the San Rafael mine in Peru's southern highlands.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
